# every release has a later one, and later is transitive; so some
# release is later than itself.  Invalid, but only an endless line of
# releases shows it: no case of any finite size does
atom	later(x,y)	y is later than x
P1	S1	all x: some y: later(x,y)
P2	S2	all x: all y: all z: later(x,y) & later(y,z) -> later(x,z)
C	S3	some x: later(x,x)
